      <title>UK sanctions Sudanese military leaders implicated in El Fasher ‘campaign of rape’</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/26/uk-sanctions-sudanese-military-leaders-implicated-in-el-fasher-campaign-of</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Commanders suspected of sexual violence during the largest and fastest slaughter of civilians in more than 30 years have been subjected to travel ban and asset freeze&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Senior Sudanese commanders implicated in a “campaign of rape” have been targeted by the UK on the first anniversary of a &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/mar/25/heroism-horror-and-the-pits-of-hell-inside-the-last-days-of-el-fasher"&gt;mass atrocity&lt;/a&gt; that saw tens of thousands of civilians killed over several days.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A year after the &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2025/nov/02/he-told-the-world-what-was-happening-in-el-fasher-then-they-sought-him-out-how-sudan-lost-a-true-hero-of-the-war"&gt;fall of El Fasher&lt;/a&gt;, the British government said it had sanctioned military leaders from both sides in the country’s ongoing conflict whom it suspected of sexual violence during the siege of the city.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/26/uk-sanctions-sudanese-military-leaders-implicated-in-el-fasher-campaign-of"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
